The logical bug is that the function doesn't check if the descriptor fields (getter, setter, value) are valid before freeing them. While this might not cause crashes due to JS_FreeValue's internal checks, it could lead to incorrect behavior if called with partially initialized descriptors.

Here's the proposed fix:

```diff
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -8855,6 +8855,9 @@
 
 static void js_free_desc(JSContext *ctx, JSPropertyDescriptor *desc)
